B.R9=new A.kq("cycle-length","A usual cycle length","ACOG calls a cycle length usual when it is 21 to 35 days, from one period start to the next. One saved date is not a completed cycle. A usual length is not a diagnosis.","ACOG menstruation ranges. EVA uses this same 21\u201335 day range on Today.")
B.R4=new A.kq("period-length","How long a period usually lasts","ACOG calls a period usual when the bleed lasts 2 to 7 days. That is the bleed length you saved, not a finding about your health.","ACOG menstruation ranges. EVA uses this same 2\u20137 day range for the period badge.")
B.R6=new A.kq("regular","When cycles are called regular","ACOG calls cycles regular when the longest and shortest differ by 7 days or less. EVA says REGULAR only after two or more measured cycles.","ACOG regularity range. One saved date is not called regular.")
B.R7=new A.kq("fertile","A fertile window is a calendar","Wilcox and colleagues (NEJM 1995) studied conception from intercourse in a six-day window ending on urine-dated ovulation, among people trying to conceive. EVA will not print that study as your personal chance. It is not contraception.","Wilcox et al., New England Journal of Medicine, 1995. Cited in EVA readings.")
B.R8=new A.kq("hormones","The hormone sketch is not a blood test","The curves are a textbook model. Nothing on that chart was measured in your blood.","EVA stamps that chart SKETCH.")
B.R3=new A.kq("pcos","A PCOS question is not a diagnosis","Reading about PCOS, including weight, does not mean you have PCOS. A clinician makes that call from more than a question.","EVA educational guidance. This app does not run a diagnostic checker.")
B.R2=new A.kq("partner","What a partner phone can hold","A partner message can carry the current phase, a daily tip, and three ways to help. Notes, logged symptoms, Ask, and these readings stay on your phone.","EVA partner sharing. The copy expires 48 hours after the code is created. It is not a live link.")
B.R5=new A.kq("urgent","If this is urgent","If this is an emergency, call local emergency services. In the US or Canada, call or text 988. Outside the US and Canada, use a local crisis line. A directory of local lines is at findahelpline.com. This app is not the emergency service.","The same emergency line EVA shows elsewhere.")
